From a178508efa31a3b03c3f428d1943628a92d0bf90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 03:30:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: find a tapped look-alike element again after the screen
 moves

A tap after a scroll waits for its element to stop moving, finding it in
each new hierarchy by its attributes. Elements that look alike, such as the
switches of a settings page that all read 1 or 0, matched more than once, so
the element counted as gone and the tap landed where it had been before the
list moved: on another row.

- refreshElement tells look-alikes apart by the ids of the elements that
  hold them in the hierarchy the element was found in, which a scroll
  doesn't change.
- An element found with childOf now carries the whole screen it was found
  on, as one found without it does, rather than a hierarchy of the element
  alone, which has no ids around it to tell look-alikes apart by.
